PROVENANCE — where this code came from
================================================================================

Ferry is a derivative work. It is not an original implementation of the AirPlay
protocol, and this file records the full chain it descends from. Nothing here is
optional attribution: each link below is a licensing obligation.

1. mazer666/PhairPlay
   <https://github.com/mazer666/PhairPlay>

   Ferry is derived directly from PhairPlay, an AirPlay 2 receiver for Android TV
   and Fire TV. The Kotlin application — RTSP handling, the AirPlay 2 handshake,
   mDNS advertisement, the MediaCodec video pipeline, the service architecture,
   and the TV user interface — originates there. PhairPlay's repository declared
   the Apache License 2.0.

   See LICENSING NOTE below regarding that declaration.

2. FDH2/UxPlay  and  FD-/RPiPlay
   <https://github.com/FDH2/UxPlay>
   <https://github.com/FD-/RPiPlay>

   PhairPlay's AirPlay implementation derives from UxPlay, which derives in turn
   from RPiPlay. The FairPlay key-decryption code in app/src/main/cpp/playfair/
   reached Ferry through RPiPlay's lib/playfair. RPiPlay is licensed under the GNU
   General Public License version 3.

   Both RPiPlay and UxPlay ship byte-identical copies of these files; Ferry's
   copies of playfair.c, playfair.h, omg_hax.c, omg_hax.h and hand_garble.c are
   byte-for-byte identical to that upstream. modified_md5.c and sap_hash.c carry
   small portability fixes (strict-aliasing and unaligned-access corrections)
   inherited from PhairPlay; see AUDIT.md for the complete diff.

3. EstebanKubata/playfair
   <https://github.com/EstebanKubata/playfair>

   The original FairPlay implementation. RPiPlay's README credits its lib/playfair
   directory to this project, and EstebanKubata/playfair is licensed GPLv3.

   This is the root of the GPL obligation that determines Ferry's license: the
   FairPlay code is GPLv3 at its origin, and every project that redistributed it
   downstream (RPiPlay, UxPlay) is likewise GPLv3.

4. openairplay/airplay-spec
   <https://github.com/openairplay/airplay-spec>

   Protocol documentation for AirPlay and AirPlay 2 — the reverse-engineered
   description of the RTSP handshake, pairing, and stream formats that these
   implementations are built against.

